note:
In the first test case, there are 5≥3 possible ways to choose the sets:

S1 — both 1 and 2 are included in S1;
S1 and S2 — 1 is included in S1 and S2, and 2 is included in S1;
S1 and S3 — 1 is included in S1, and 2 is included in S1 and S3;
S2 and S3 — 1 is included in S2, and 2 is included in S3;
S1, S2, and S3 — 1 is included in S1 and S2, and 2 is included in S1 and S3.

Note that it is invalid to choose S2 only because 2 is not included in S2.

In the second test case, the only way is to choose all the sets.

In the third test case, 5 does not appear in any of the sets, so there is no way to choose the sets.

In the fourth test case, choosing any non-empty collection of the sets is valid, so the number of ways is 25−1=31≥3.
